---
import { BleedImage, Slide } from '@decks';

import architecture from '../images/architecture.png?url';

// Image-led. The diagram carries the slide and the decisions get spoken
// over it: why four packages rather than one, lockstep versioning and
// what it cost, and why npm was the distribution channel.
//
// The metrics that used to sit here in a facts row moved to
// 2-Impact.astro. Splitting the numbers across three slides meant none of
// them landed.
//
// Source is 1973x1127, so aspect 1.751, near enough 16:9 that it wants
// most of the slide. Scaled to 1541x880 and bled off the bottom: the
// aspect matches the source exactly so object-cover crops nothing. The
// diagram's own content starts about 7% down and ends about 92% down, so
// on the slide it runs roughly y=259 to y=1008, clear of the header and
// with the image's own bottom whitespace absorbing the bleed.
//
// Matches the treatment on 4-FigmaComponents.astro so the two
// consumption slides read as a pair.
---

<Slide subtitle="Architecture">
	<BleedImage
		src={architecture}
		alt="Anvil architecture. Tokens, an icon set, and fonts feed a React and CSS component library. Each is compiled and published to npm as @servicetitan/tokens, anvil-icons, anvil-fonts, and anvil, then consumed by the desktop app. The component library also produces documentation, Storybook, and html-sketchapp output that flows through Abstract into Sketch."
		bleed="bottom"
		class="h-[880px] w-[1541px] object-cover"
	/>
</Slide>
